{"name":"Gala Ball","hex":"#785d7a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gala","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Celebratory; festive."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Pomp, show, or festivity.","A competition."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gala"},{"term":"ball","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A solid or hollow sphere, or roughly spherical mass.","A quantity of string, thread, etc., wound into a spherical shape."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form or wind into a ball.","To heat in a furnace and form into balls for rolling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ball"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ball","blocks":[{"text":"A ball is a round object. Balls can have several uses. For example they are used in ball games, where the play of the game follows the state of the ball as it is hit, kicked or thrown by players. Balls can also be used for simpler activities, such as catch or juggling. Balls made from hard-wearing materials are used in engineering applications to provide very low friction bearings, known as ball bearings. Black-powder weapons use stone and metal balls as projectiles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Many_balls.jpg/330px-Many_balls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ball","wikidata":"Q18545"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Balls_-_10-15c_-_Novgorod_Kremlin_Museum.jpg/500px-Balls_-_10-15c_-_Novgorod_Kremlin_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Balls_-_10-15c_-_Novgorod_Kremlin_Museum.jpg/1280px-Balls_-_10-15c_-_Novgorod_Kremlin_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Balls_-_10-15c_-_Novgorod_Kremlin_Mu